   "id": 669399,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\">\n    <li>Here is the graph of quadratic function <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>.</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p><img height=\"139\" src=\"exercises/media/eee8bbe006f3a8b1.svg\" width=\"153\" alt=\"A parabola on a coordinate plane with x and y axes. The x-axis includes markings for -4, 4, and 8. The y-axis includes markings for -8, 8, and 16. A point is marked at the vertex of the parabola with coordinates five, negative seven.\"></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Andre uses the expression <span data-math=\"(x−5)^2+7\">(x−5)^2+7</span> to define <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Noah uses the expression <span data-math=\"(x+5)^2−7\">(x+5)^2−7</span> to define <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>.</p></li>\n  </ul><p>Do you agree with either of them?&nbsp;</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1334321,
     "content_html": "Yes"
    },
    {
     "id": 1334322,
     "content_html": "No"
    }
   ],
